4. Assess demand vs channel-stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return rate at the anomaly month vs the 24-month average return rate for that combo, (b) whether the following 1-3 months show a sharp drop (reversal), (c) whether the spike is isolated or part of a trend. Save a structured assessment table to offline_data/anomaly_assessment.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded data: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing top-3 anomalies with multiples, months, return rates; (3) every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is real demand or channel stuffing; (5) no external data, only from the local CSV. → code_agent
